Despite their loyalty and companionship, not every dog is able to form a close bond with its human owner.   尽管狗很忠诚且富有陪伴性，但并不是每只狗都能与它的主人建立亲密的关系。
Adopting a family pet requires not only time and care but also a long-term commitment to the animal’s well-being.   收养一只家庭宠物不仅需要时间和关爱，还需要对动物福祉做出长期承诺。
Service animals such as hearing dogs or mobility assistance animals also require extensive training and are often matched carefully with individuals based on personality and needs.   诸如助听犬或行动辅助犬等服务动物同样需要大量的训练，并且通常会根据个性和需求与个人进行仔细匹配。
Researchers in Germany are also exploring how personality assessments for both dogs and their owners can improve long-term compatibility.   德国的研究人员还正在探索如何通过对狗和其主人的性格评估来提高长期的相容性。
Many pet owners often joke that their dogs have inherited not just their personality, but also their facial expressions.   许多宠物主人都开玩笑说，他们的狗不仅继承了他们的性格，还有他们的面部表情。
People who share common interests and values often find it easier to build and maintain deep, long-term relationships.   拥有共同兴趣和价值观的人往往更容易建立并维持深厚而长久的关系。
People often choose pets that reflect their personalities, such as active individuals preferring energetic breeds or quiet individuals opting for more laid-back companions.   人们常常会选择与自己性格相符的宠物，例如，活跃的人倾向于选择精力充沛的品种，而安静的人则更喜欢性格温顺的伴侣。
People who lead sedentary lifestyles often find that their pets are more likely to become sedentary as well.   那些过着久坐生活方式的人往往会发现他们的宠物也更容易变得不爱活动。
Studies have also found that people tend to unconsciously mimic the body language and gestures of those they feel close to.   研究还发现，人们往往会无意识地模仿他们亲近的人的身体语言和手势。
Owners often choose dog breeds that align with their own lifestyles and energy levels, which can influence how active or reserved their pets become.   主人往往会根据自己的生活方式和精力水平选择犬种，这会影响他们的宠物变得活跃或内向。
People who score high in openness tend to have more playful and curious dogs, while those with low empathy may find it harder to bond with their pets.   在“开放性”方面得分较高的人往往拥有更爱玩、更好奇的狗，而共情能力较低的人可能更难与他们的宠物建立情感联系。
